@alife-records 1

node vp_1084.VQ_HOUSE_BATH
  t.any.1 A basin would be welcome.. clean hands might improve my mood
  t.any.2 Yes please.. have no wish to leave muddy fingerprints on everything
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_HOUSE_BED
  t.any.1 Would like to lie down.. might stop rehearsing conversations I haven't had
  t.any.2 Yes.. no need to fuss over the bedding on my account
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_HOUSE_PHONE
  t.any.1 Could try a neighbor if a line works.. no close family to call
  t.any.2 Not certain whom I'd reach.. please don't dial anyone just to keep me occupied
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_HOUSE_QUIET
  t.any.1 Would prefer television sound.. quiet lets me repeat myself far too clearly
  t.any.2 Quiet can be tiring.. listen to that sentence, ridiculous but correct
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_HOUSE_SHELF
  t.any.1 May look?.. my own paperback needs drying more than reading
  t.any.2 Something comic, if there is any.. not a lesson in endurance
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_HOUSE_TV
  t.lo.1 Yes.. exactly what I hoped to ask
  t.mid.1 Please try it.. would be grateful for something other than warnings
  t.hi.1 Yes!.. if music comes on, leave it there.. don't explain why the news is more useful
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_HOUSE_WELCOME
  t.any.1 Thank you.. will try not to behave as if I'm waiting for a pupil
  t.any.2 Very well.. somewhere to put the damp book would help me settle
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_CARRYING
  t.any.1 A book swollen by rain.. it was a comedy before it became a sponge
  t.any.2 Pen, comb, letters.. no metronome, finally free of its judgment
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_FUTURE
  gate.rule trust>=76 & alone & flag:device_told
  t.hi.1 Want music on television.. might remember my tap steps.. Mrs. Wiles taught me secretly from sixty-one to sixty-seven, while I told Mother I only accompanied.. yes, TAP.. don't look as if you've caught me stealing the piano.. I'd like to enjoy it again
  fx.1 reveal f_tap
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d
  t.any.1 A program worth watching would be a start
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d2
  t.any.1 Not planning a respectable little routine for your approval
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d3
  t.any.1 Let tomorrow remain my decision, please
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_HELP
  t.any.1 Could read something difficult aloud.. or write a letter as dictated, without correcting the sender
  t.any.2 Not a repairman.. could mend a small tear, Mother made certain of that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_HURT
  t.any.1 A little sore from traveling.. you can have a look if you're concerned
  t.any.2 Ache a little.. please don't promote it into an emergency on my behalf
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_PLAN
  gate.rule !flag:pupils_told
  t.any.1 Somewhere to stop and hear the television.. traveled alone, can decide for myself
  t.any.2 Find a room.. came alone, no household following me in
  t.any.3 I have no itinerary. That is an admission, not a request for one
  t.any.4 One sensible choice would do. I'm not attempting to conduct the whole county
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_PLAN.a2
  gate.rule flag:pupils_told
  t.any.1 A stopping place for now.. no longer pretending I set out alone
  t.any.2 Don't know what the road holds.. keep seeing Mr. Pike's coat when I try to decide
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_ROAD
  gate.rule trust>=12
  t.any.1 Bad crossing.. been claiming I came alone, but offered to escort two former pupils, Beatrice Holm, forty-nine, and Lewis Pike, fifty-two.. fear stopped me at a footbridge.. took another route and left them there without help.. don't know what happened to them.. remember Mr. Pike's coat across his arm
  fx.1 reveal f_pupils
  fx.2 set flag:pupils_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_ROAD.d
  t.any.1 Came by the longer way.. don't want to walk it again in words
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_ROAD.d2
  t.any.1 There was a crossing.. enough about the road for now
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_ROAD.d3
  t.any.1 Stop asking me to picture the bridge
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_THIRSTY
  t.any.1 Yes, water would be welcome.. have done too much talking on too little
  t.any.2 Thirsty.. had a small drink while stopping, not nearly enough
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_TIRED
  t.any.1 Last slept in scraps at a stopping place.. need something better than scraps
  t.any.2 Would like rest.. could fall asleep in the middle of correcting a sentence, a genuine advance
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_WANT
  t.any.1 Television.. sound from a program, even a foolish one
  t.any.2 Would like to hear ordinary voices from the TV.. not another account of what I ought to do
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_WASH
  t.any.1 Yes.. hands and face first, if I may
  t.any.2 Would like to wash.. my cuffs have brought an unnecessary amount of roadside dirt
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_WORRY
  gate.rule trust>=60 & alone & flag:sunday_told
  t.hi.1 My heart.. have a pacemaker, implanted in ninety.. kept it from acquaintances because I couldn't bear all the supervision they'd offer.. not asking you to fix it, telling you why I dislike being managed
  fx.1 reveal f_device
  fx.2 set flag:device_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_WORRY.d
  t.any.1 Health among other worries.. not asking for an examination
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_WORRY.d2
  t.any.1 Don't want a committee appointed to supervise me
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_NOW_WORRY.d3
  t.any.1 My health is not permission to take charge of me
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_OFFER_BED
  t.any.1 Yes.. an offer I needn't correct
  t.any.2 Could use a place to sleep.. not particular about grand names for the furniture
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_OFFER_BOOK
  t.any.1 Would look.. preferably a book with pages still the right thickness
  t.any.2 A comedy would be welcome.. can't promise not to read a good line aloud
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_OFFER_DRINK
  t.any.1 Yes please.. something to drink, no ceremony
  t.any.2 Water would suit me.. ought to have interrupted my own talking to ask
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_DAYONE
  t.any.1 Near Middlesboro, trying to reach transport.. prefer not to summarize it as an adventure
  t.any.2 Away from my piano.. rain got into my paperback while I was traveling
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_FAMILY
  t.lo.1 No wife or children.. Mother and my brother Francis have both died
  t.mid.1 Never married.. former pupils became the people who called round
  t.hi.1 No close family waiting that I know of.. Mother died in seventy-four, Francis in eighty-eight
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_FIRSTJOB
  t.any.1 Piano lessons for a neighbor, Mrs. Adler.. she wanted one particular waltz
  t.any.2 Accompanying practice and taking beginners.. good way to discover how slowly an hour could pass
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_HOBBY
  t.any.1 Letters after lessons.. made a fresh page seem a fairly large undertaking
  t.any.2 Fishing sometimes.. winning the derby rather ruined peaceful anonymity
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_HOUSE
  t.any.1 Front room had the piano.. pupils always arrived through the wrong door
  t.any.2 A narrow house with a very audible stair.. privacy depended on people choosing not to listen
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_LOVE
  t.any.1 Never married.. not every solitary man has a tragic lost sweetheart
  t.any.2 Had attachments.. none became a household, and no one owes me an explanation now
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_MENTOR
  t.any.1 First piano teacher, Miss Bell.. insisted that listening counted as work
  t.any.2 Doris Wiles taught me how an accompanist should wait.. no one could hurry that woman
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_PARENTS
  t.any.1 Both dead.. cared for Madeline, my mother, in her last years
  t.any.2 Mother lived to ninety.. born eighty-four of the last century, died seventy-four of this one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_PROUD
  t.any.1 A pupil playing a tune without waiting for my nod.. preferred not to let them see how pleased I was
  t.any.2 That fishing prize in eighty-one.. shamelessly displayed the badge where piano pupils could see it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_REGRET
  gate.rule trust>=44 & alone & flag:francis_told
  t.hi.1 Promised Mother a Sunday at the lake.. kept accepting paid lessons instead and postponing it.. Madeline died in seventy-four, ninety years old, without that trip.. couldn't put one afternoon ahead of being wanted at the piano
  fx.1 reveal f_sunday
  fx.2 set flag:sunday_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d
  t.any.1 A promise to Mother.. won't make it into a pretty memory
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d2
  t.any.1 Not telling that one to have someone forgive it quickly
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d3
  t.any.1 No.. don't offer me a different Sunday in its place
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  t.any.1 Local school, then further music study.. piano was the part I wanted to keep
  t.any.2 Studied music.. could pass a written examination more readily than play while somebody watched
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_SIBLING
  gate.rule trust>=28 & alone & flag:pupils_told
  t.hi.1 Francis, four years older.. stopped answering him when he urged a care home for Mother.. called it interference.. he died in eighty-eight and I still hadn't answered.. have his last letter, no one left to post the reply to
  fx.1 reveal f_francis
  fx.2 set flag:francis_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_SIBLING.d
  t.any.1 Francis, my older brother.. died in eighty-eight
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_SIBLING.d2
  t.any.1 Our correspondence is not ready for reading aloud
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_SIBLING.d3
  t.any.1 No inspection of the envelope.. leave it alone
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_TOWN
  t.any.1 Middlesboro.. knew people by what they hummed as much as by their faces
  t.any.2 Had my usual walk.. never grew fond of the crossings just because they were familiar
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_TRAVEL
  t.any.1 Some travel for music.. liked arriving considerably more than crossing the bridges on the way
  t.any.2 Not a seasoned traveler.. my letters went farther than I did
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_PAST_WORK
  t.any.1 Private piano teacher.. retired from regular lessons in ninety-one
  t.any.2 Taught piano and accompanied dance classes.. not a schoolmaster, despite the manner
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_ADVICE
  t.any.1 If you write a letter, post it before you improve it beyond recognition
  t.any.2 Listen to the whole question.. not an accusation, merely advice I often needed
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Seventy-six.. nineteen seventeen, if you prefer the arithmetic
  t.any.2 Seventy-six.. younger than the yellow metronome sounded by the end
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 Calling piano practice a waste of time, then requesting a tune at every gathering
  t.any.2 A letter beginning with no salutation.. at least identify whom you're cross with
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.lo.1 Bridges.. dislike seeing what is underneath my feet
  t.mid.1 A bridge can be perfectly sound and still stop me.. an infuriating distinction
  t.hi.1 Don't tell me not to look down.. have thought of that in seventy-six years
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 Peach preserves on fresh bread.. was quite capable of spoiling my appetite with it
  t.any.2 Roast chicken.. skin left on, please, I'm not studying virtue at supper
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.any.1 Middlesboro.. born there, never learned to call somewhere else home
  t.any.2 From Middlesboro.. took a longer route than I meant to
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Smoothing the book.. rain made the pages too thick for their own cover
  t.any.2 Counting on my fingers.. before you ask, no, not your grammatical errors
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.any.1 An ordinary program coming on.. somebody else deciding what happens for half an hour
  t.any.2 Hope my piano is still dry.. won't add a sermon about hope to that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Unsettled.. would rather hear an ordinary television voice than my own thoughts
  t.mid.1 Damp and irritable.. no, those are separate complaints
  t.mid.2 Well enough to answer, though I reserve the right to revise it
  t.mid.3 I would prefer an ordinary conversation to an assessment of my condition
  t.mid.4 Rather better when you don't assume I need an improving thought
  t.hi.1 Want something enjoyable.. there, not a lesson or a worthy use of time
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_JOKE
  t.any.1 A pupil asked if practice made perfect.. said it made the neighbors informed
  t.any.2 Madeline wanted me to learn a useful instrument.. suggested a dinner bell
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 Writing letters.. receiving an answer without a corrected spelling is a rare pleasure
  t.any.2 Comedy read aloud.. the yellow metronome never developed a sense of humor
  t.any.3 Playing something for the pleasure of it, with nobody asking what it teaches
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Piano, of course.. like a tune people recognize without being told to admire it
  t.any.2 Music with a clear rhythm.. dislike listening to someone merely demonstrate difficulty
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Everett Bishop.. Mr. Bishop at lessons, Everett elsewhere
  t.any.2 Bishop, Everett.. sorry, still answer as though someone is checking a register
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_NERVOUS
  t.any.1 Yes.. repeating a sentence aloud sometimes settles me
  t.any.2 Quite.. would appreciate not having to deny the obvious
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Yes.. unless I start reading aloud, in which case you may object
  t.any.2 Would like that.. have corrected quite enough of my own thoughts
  t.any.3 Gladly. You need not mistake a pause for an invitation to advise me
  t.any.4 Stay if you wish. It is possible to enjoy company without performing for it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Poorly.. start composing a letter and reach sunrise at the salutation
  t.any.2 A little sleep at a stopping place.. don't dignify it as a full night
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_SPORTS
  t.any.1 Heard Wildcats games on the radio.. shouted corrections nobody requested
  t.any.2 Won a fishing derby in eighty-one.. my entire claim to sporting distinction
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.mid.1 Mrs. Wiles once made me play the same bar twelve times.. finally admitted her shoe buckle was stuck
  t.hi.1 Doris Wiles taught dancing.. once kept her class circling while I repeated four bars, all because her shoe buckle wouldn't open.. Mrs. Wiles called it endurance training
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_TALK_TV
  t.any.1 Musical programs.. old comedies too, when they let a joke finish
  t.any.2 Would enjoy the television.. don't need it to improve my character
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_WORLD_HOPE
  t.any.1 Old routines might keep us going.. something done at the proper time
  t.any.2 Want to think the old ways still work.. wanting is not the same as an answer
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Only what I heard while leaving.. have no later reliable report
  t.any.2 Nothing new.. have been listening harder than I've been learning
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.VQ_WORLD_PLANS
  t.any.1 Would look for underground shelter.. haven't tested that notion, won't call it a guarantee
  t.any.2 I'd favor somewhere enclosed over another crossing.. my fear may be doing the planning there
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1084.leave.angry
  t.any.1 No further discussion.. perfectly correct use of the word further
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1084.leave.grateful
  t.any.1 Thank you.. an inadequate sentence, but for once I'll leave it alone
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1084.leave.need_met
  t.any.1 You've helped with what I needed.. would spoil the thanks by adding an essay
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1084.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Book, comb, pen.. yes, finished checking, goodbye
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1084.react.compliment
  t.any.1 Oh.. thank you.. rather disarms the reply I was preparing
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.gave_book
  t.any.1 A book to keep?.. thank you, will try to keep this one dry
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.gave_clothes
  t.any.1 Will try the fit.. my cuffs can hardly object to competition
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.gave_food
  t.any.1 Thank you.. kind to share when everything's become so uncertain
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.gave_water
  t.any.1 Thank you.. a sensible thing to offer a man who keeps talking
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.ignored
  t.any.1 Bishop is still attempting a conversation.. perhaps unwisely
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.insult
  t.any.1 You needn't like me.. could still manage a civil sentence
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.offered_bed
  t.any.1 Would like that.. fatigue has made me a very repetitive correspondent
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.refused
  t.any.1 Understood.. won't search for a different meaning in a clear answer
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.sorry
  t.any.1 All right.. apologies aren't examinations, I know
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.thanks
  t.any.1 You're welcome.. shall accept that without improving its wording
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.react.threat
  t.any.1 Leaving.. do not need that repeated more loudly
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1084.return.arrive
  t.any.1 Everett Bishop again.. no formal introduction necessary this time
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1084.return.gave_food
  gate.rule gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Remember you sharing food.. composed a thank-you in my head, keep making it longer by editing it
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1084.return.refused_door
  t.any.1 May I ask about admission now?.. remember the earlier answer, not disputing it
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1084.return.threatened
  t.any.1 Keeping my distance.. have not forgotten why I left before
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1090.VE_WASH_UP.prompt
  gate.rule need:dirty>=3 & (poi:sink | poi:bath) & imin>=30
  t.any.1 May I rinse these cuffs?.. register can wait somewhere dry
  tag.1 kind:event
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_BATH
  t.any.1 Gladly.. how much water may I use on the cuffs?
  t.any.2 Register needs a dry place before I start washing
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_CHAIR
  t.any.1 Good chair?.. another one will do if that's somebody's usual seat
  t.any.2 Thank you.. may the register rest beside it?
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_CHORES
  t.any.1 Figures if you have accounts.. not a census of your belongings
  t.any.2 Can fold clean cloths.. mind the margin on this register if it's nearby
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_PHONE
  t.any.1 Would try Ruth at her sister's.. may I use it?
  t.any.2 Raymond's number is inside the register.. could try him after Ruth
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_PRAYER
  t.any.1 Yes.. for Ruth by name rather than for my own arrangements
  t.any.2 A minute's enough to begin.. needn't fill the silence afterward
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_SHELF
  t.any.1 Large print if there's any.. wouldn't mind football instead of a sermon
  t.any.2 May I look at the titles before choosing?
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_STOVE
  t.any.1 Would like that.. is there heat in it or just a place to sit?
  t.any.2 Near it please.. won't presume the stove's lit for my benefit
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_HOUSE_WELCOME
  t.any.1 Thank you.. won't appoint myself to arrange your chairs
  t.any.2 Show me a place for the register.. not another person's place
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_CARRYING
  t.any.1 Register and pencil.. ribbon pressed inside
  t.any.2 Spectacles and too many keys for the doors I can still reach
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_GLASSES
  gate.rule trust>=10
  t.any.1 Not as well as these glasses suggest.. doctor said cataracts in ninety-one.. hid the diagnosis from the committee and kept moving meetings into daylight
  fx.1 reveal f_eyes
  fx.2 set flag:eyes_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_GLASSES.d
  t.any.1 Better in daylight.. let me find the right angle
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_GLASSES.d2
  t.any.1 My spectacles don't entitle anyone to the whole medical paper
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_HELP
  t.any.1 Can put figures in order if there's daylight
  t.any.2 Room arrangements.. only after you tell me what you actually need
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY
  t.any.1 Not badly.. enough food to stop thinking about the next request
  t.any.2 Could manage a little.. Pearl never approved of leaving it too late
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_HURT
  t.any.1 Shoes could use mercy.. would you check where they're rubbing?
  t.any.2 Would like to stop walking awhile.. take a look before I go again
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_PLAN
  t.any.1 Warmth first.. then somewhere I can leave Ruth a message
  t.any.2 Not going back just to put the chairs straight
  t.any.3 I'd like to know what's possible before I say what we're doing. What I'm doing
  t.any.4 Nothing settled. Please don't hear that as a request to decide for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_THIRSTY
  t.any.1 A little water please.. would ask where it's from
  t.any.2 Water from a source you know.. not asking you to certify the county
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_TIRED
  t.any.1 Last sleep was that church pew.. only a few hours
  t.any.2 Pew edge woke me before the bell.. don't know which I resented more
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_TRUST
  t.lo.1 Would answer a name.. not hand over the register
  t.mid.1 Less inclined to put a margin round every answer
  t.hi.1 Could admit the register isn't the same as knowing people
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_WANT
  t.any.1 A place near warmth.. no claim on your whole stove
  t.any.2 Need to stop with the register somewhere dry and warm
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_NOW_WASH
  t.any.1 Yes.. cuffs first and the register clear of splashes
  t.any.2 Road dust ought to stay on the road.. where may I rinse?
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_OFFER_BLANKET
  t.any.1 That may help more than hovering near a stove
  t.any.2 If it's available.. will keep the register's pencil off it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_OFFER_BOOK
  t.any.1 Borrow one with readable print.. may I choose?
  t.any.2 Could return it before I leave.. easier than carrying another account
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_OFFER_FOOD
  t.any.1 A little please.. only what's actually spare
  t.any.2 Yes.. don't need Ruth's table to accept a meal
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_CHURCH
  gate.rule trust>=55 & alone & flag:tomatoes_told
  t.any.1 Kept the church accounts.. then kept the cellar coal and tins for members on my list.. turned neighborhood people away because their names weren't in our register
  fx.1 reveal f_cellar
  fx.2 set flag:cellar_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_CHURCH.d
  t.any.1 Deacon at the Louisville church.. cellar's not an easy subject
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_CHURCH.d2
  t.any.1 Not opening that door for an audience
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_DAYONE
  t.any.1 At church checking the register.. left it open when the first shouting started
  t.any.2 Put chairs into rows before anybody had asked for rows.. old habits first
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_FAMILY
  t.any.1 Ruth's my wife.. staying with her sister when I last knew
  t.any.2 Raymond's my nephew.. no children of our own
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_FIRSTJOB
  t.any.1 Wrapping hinges beside Benton.. paper cut worse than the metal
  t.any.2 First wages bought Pearl a proper pair of cuff buttons
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_HOBBY
  t.any.1 Football on paper.. Raymond used to explain the rules over cold tea
  t.any.2 Garden watching.. Ruth said it wasn't the same as gardening
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_HOUSE
  t.any.1 Three narrow rooms.. Ruth made the space outside count
  t.any.2 Garden gate caught every tie I owned.. learned to tuck them in
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_LOVE
  t.any.1 Ruth.. married in fifty-eight.. she chose yellow for the kitchen
  t.any.2 Still married.. living apart isn't something a neat answer fixes
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_MENTOR
  t.any.1 Benton taught labels.. Mina taught me a list can still be wrong
  t.any.2 Raymond taught me to lose at football without changing the rules
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_PARENTS
  t.any.1 Pearl kept shirts going.. Benton packed hardware till his hands objected
  t.any.2 Mother died in eighty-one.. still hear her objecting to these cuffs
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_PROUD
  gate.rule trust>=40 & alone & flag:lessons_told
  t.any.1 Garden ribbon.. should say Ruth's ribbon.. she raised those tomatoes from her seedlings in eighty-nine.. entered them under my name and stood taking the praise
  fx.1 reveal f_tomatoes
  fx.2 set flag:tomatoes_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_PROUD.d
  t.any.1 There's a ribbon in the register.. pride's not quite the word
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_PROUD.d2
  t.any.1 Leave the garden account until I can give Ruth her due
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_REGRET
  gate.rule trust>=70 & alone & flag:cellar_told
  t.any.1 Promised Mina a committee vote on letting the excluded neighbors share the cellar supplies.. tore their petition out before the meeting.. no vote ever had a chance
  cb.1 Mina's petition.. should have put it before them instead of deciding who counted
  fx.1 reveal f_petition
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d
  t.any.1 Mina asked something of me I haven't answered honestly yet
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d2
  t.any.1 That torn edge isn't a subject I'm ready to finish
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  gate.rule trust>=25 & flag:eyes_told
  t.any.1 Completion course.. graduated in eighty-five.. Raymond read the lessons aloud till I could follow them.. accepted the congratulations without giving him his part
  fx.1 reveal f_lessons
  fx.2 set flag:lessons_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d
  t.any.1 Evening course.. the certificate's at home
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d2
  t.any.1 Raymond's help deserves a proper telling.. not yet
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_TRAVEL
  t.any.1 Little outside Louisville except church visits
  t.any.2 Longest ordinary trip was for Raymond's wedding.. wore the shortened tie
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_PAST_WORK
  t.lo.1 Deacon.. accounts and repairs, not the sermon
  t.mid.1 Packed hardware before the church needed my daylight
  t.hi.1 Arranged the rooms and names.. liked arrangements more than I understood people
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Fifty-nine.. born before Benton could afford the fourth chair
  t.any.2 Thirty-four was my year.. Raymond keeps the football years for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 A register with no room beside the name
  t.any.2 Being handed a list already called unanimous
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.any.1 Church bells now.. can't hear one without waiting for the next
  t.any.2 That bell in Louisville kept ringing after anybody needed calling
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 Tomato on bread.. Ruth always salted it after the first taste
  t.any.2 Pearl's baked onions.. difficult to praise with a full mouth
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.any.1 Louisville.. behind a church garden that Ruth planted
  t.any.2 Narrow house near the church.. the garden made it seem wider
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Cracking my knuckles.. Benton did it before opening a difficult letter
  t.any.2 Mind the margin.. hands keep searching for a bit of paper to straighten
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.any.1 Ruth answering for herself wherever she is
  t.any.2 A warm place without having to set up its committee
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Knuckles keep cracking.. rest of me's quieter
  t.lo.2 Cuffs survived Louisville better than my shoes
  t.mid.1 For my part.. tired of arranging where people ought to sit
  t.mid.2 Register feels heavier when I stop moving
  t.mid.3 We manage. I manage, I mean; I shouldn't answer for everybody
  t.mid.4 Don't quite know. I've been arranging the answer instead of giving it
  t.mid.5 A little easier to say when you're not waiting for something reassuring
  t.hi.1 Can leave a question unanswered for a moment.. that's new
  t.hi.2 Less need to say we're managing when I only mean me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 Paper football league with Raymond.. Sunday columns for something harmless
  t.any.2 Ruth's garden before the judging starts
  t.any.3 Having a small job finished and not immediately being handed another
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Piano before the service.. while the room's still deciding to settle
  t.any.2 Ruth singing from the garden.. couldn't always make out the words
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Douglas Holbrook.. Douglas will do in a house
  t.any.2 Holbrook.. no need for Deacon ahead of it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_NERVOUS
  t.any.1 Yes.. an unexpected bell can make me lose the whole room
  t.any.2 Keep checking whether the register's folded shut.. needn't check it for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_PRAYER
  t.any.1 Still try.. silence after it hasn't changed
  t.any.2 For my part.. would like an answer I hadn't put there myself
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Yes.. hands may take longer to agree
  t.any.2 Register can remain closed while neither of us talks
  t.any.3 Yes. I needn't find something helpful to say every time you look over
  t.any.4 You can stay without giving me a reason. I'd prefer that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Last proper stretch was in a pew.. woke with the register under my elbow
  t.any.2 Sleep comes between the sounds I mistake for bells
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_SPORTS
  t.any.1 Raymond and I chose football teams on paper.. no money changing hands
  t.any.2 Sunday columns are football totals too.. nephew insists on a different pencil
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.any.1 Raymond put my football team down as Garden Committee.. won that week.. Ruth asked if winning meant we'd finally weed the actual garden.. we did before looking at the scores again
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Might rain.. Ruth read the garden better than I read clouds
  t.any.2 I'd welcome a cooler road.. cuffs could bear another washing
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_WORLD_CHURCH
  t.any.1 Our doors were being used when I left.. not a promise they remain open
  t.any.2 Can't name an open church from current knowledge.. register doesn't give me that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_WORLD_CITY
  t.any.1 Louisville had people walking with house keys ready.. as if the next door would be theirs
  t.any.2 Left more shouting than traffic behind.. couldn't say what streets are usable now
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_WORLD_HOPE
  t.any.1 Don't know when it ends.. Raymond would ask what I meant by ends
  t.any.2 Would like another garden season.. can't turn wanting into a date
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Heard water blamed outside Louisville.. have no proof beyond people saying it
  t.any.2 My latest certain news is a bell ringing.. can't tell you who pulled the rope
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.VQ_WORLD_WATER
  t.any.1 Church tap ran when I left.. can't answer for this house
  t.any.2 Don't know which places still have water.. suspect the water's part of this but suspicion isn't a test
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1090.leave.angry
  t.any.1 No committee to appoint here.. I'm leaving
  t.any.2 Douglas can end a visit without deciding the last word
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1090.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Register closed.. better take my questions along
  t.any.2 Tie tucked away.. garden gates aren't the only things that catch it
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1090.react.gave_book
  gate.rule gave:book
  t.any.1 Pencil's for my register.. won't bring it to these margins
  t.any.2 Raymond would check whether I'd chosen football.. let him wonder
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1090.react.gave_food
  gate.rule gave:food
  t.any.1 Thank you.. Pearl would tell me to quit qualifying that
  t.any.2 Food belongs in my thanks.. not in another column of favors
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1090.react.gave_water
  gate.rule gave:water
  t.any.1 I'll keep the register away from this
  t.any.2 Grateful for the water.. still ought to ask its source
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1090.react.insult
  t.any.1 May be better if Douglas says nothing for a moment
  t.any.2 Cuffs don't take offense.. rest of me needs a little longer
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1090.react.refused
  t.any.1 Understood.. won't call a refusal a committee matter
  t.any.2 Then that request is finished.. hands can stop counting it
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1090.react.threat
  t.any.1 Register stays closed.. show me where you want my hands
  t.any.2 Lord.. not reaching for any key.. I'll wait
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1090.return.arrive
  gate.rule visits>=1
  t.any.1 Douglas again.. register has gathered another fold
  t.any.2 Remembered this entrance without Raymond directing me
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1090.return.gave_food
  gate.rule visits>=1 & gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Food you gave me stayed in mind.. no tally needed
  t.any.2 Didn't need Sunday columns to remember being helped here
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1097.VE_WASH_UP.prompt
  gate.rule need:dirty>=3 & (poi:sink | poi:bath) & imin>=30
  t.any.1 Can I wash the road off?.. bread cloth needs a rinse too if there's spare water
  tag.1 kind:event
end

node vp_1097.VQ_HOUSE_BATH
  t.any.1 Point me to the water.. won't wander through looking for it
  t.any.2 Glad of a wash before I fold this cloth again
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_HOUSE_BED
  t.any.1 Would lie down awhile.. wake me before it becomes the whole day
  t.any.2 Bed's welcome if it's free.. had enough of that truck buckle
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_HOUSE_CHAIR
  t.any.1 I'll take the offered seat.. no great refusal from me
  t.any.2 That would do.. jacket can stay in my lap
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_HOUSE_CHORES
  t.any.1 Could sweep the shavings if you permit carving
  t.any.2 Light carrying.. don't send me up a ladder to prove something
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_HOUSE_PRAYER
  t.any.1 Yes.. would you rather I kept it to myself?
  t.any.2 A quiet minute for Luther.. not a service in your kitchen
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_HOUSE_RADIO
  t.any.1 Please.. a road report before any music
  t.any.2 Want to hear whether anybody mentions fuel.. turn it where you think best
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_HOUSE_WELCOME
  t.any.1 Where may the jacket go?.. crumbs don't need your floor
  t.any.2 Thank you.. Jeremiah isn't taking charge of your supper
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_CARRYING
  t.any.1 Keys and Luther's directions.. empty bread cloth
  t.any.2 Spoon without a proper bowl yet.. pencil to remind me where to stop cutting
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_HELP
  t.any.1 Can carry a light load after resting
  t.any.2 Read a letter aloud if you want.. won't add a sermon to it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY
  t.lo.1 Yes.. bread would do well
  t.lo.2 Cloth's empty.. won't keep unfolding it to make the answer longer
  t.mid.1 Hungry and too proud about asking twice in one day
  t.hi.1 Feed Jeremiah please.. Reverend can wait his turn
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_HURT
  t.any.1 Feet ache.. jacket rubs the back of my neck
  t.any.2 An old man walking farther than he meant.. would you check my legs?
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_PLAN
  t.any.1 Fuel for the pickup.. Luther's workshop after that
  t.any.2 Need the truck moving before I make another day's promises
  t.any.3 I need to choose what I can actually do. Faith doesn't draw me a road
  t.any.4 Haven't decided. I'd rather say it than make certainty another thing to carry
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_STAY
  t.any.1 An hour would change the walk back
  t.any.2 Till my feet stop making every decision.. not till Sunday
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_THIRSTY
  t.any.1 Water yes.. throat's had enough preaching for the road
  t.any.2 Would take some.. asking's easier than talking round it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_TIRED
  t.any.1 Truck cab was my last bed.. few hours before daylight
  t.any.2 Slept some in the pickup.. much better at lying still than sleeping
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_TRUST
  t.lo.1 Wouldn't leave the pickup keys with you
  t.mid.1 Could ask you to hold a place without knowing what to say in it
  t.hi.1 Trust you enough to say I disagree without getting up to preach
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_WANT
  t.any.1 Gasoline.. enough to get the red pickup going
  t.any.2 A way to carry fuel back.. keys aren't the missing part
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_NOW_WASH
  t.any.1 Yes.. this bread cloth too if the water's spare
  t.any.2 Jacket needs more than shaking.. I'll settle for hands and face
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_OFFER_BED
  t.any.1 An hour of it please.. don't hold a whole room for me
  t.any.2 Could rest without taking the blankets away with me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_OFFER_FOOD
  t.any.1 Yes.. hungry enough to skip the blessing if you want
  t.any.2 Gladly.. may ask afterward if any can go with me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_OFFER_MAP
  t.any.1 Luther's workshop first.. can show you the turn I remember
  t.any.2 Mark fuel if you know a place.. want less guessing than my directions have
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_CHURCH
  gate.rule trust>=55 & alone & flag:strike_told
  t.any.1 Led the church for years.. couldn't finish Nola's funeral sermon in eighty-eight.. got to meeting again and found I no longer believed my promise.. another preacher finished it
  fx.1 reveal f_nola
  fx.2 set flag:nola_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_CHURCH.d
  t.any.1 Baptist congregation.. Nola used to play before the service
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_CHURCH.d2
  t.any.1 Her funeral isn't a sermon for company
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_DAYONE
  t.any.1 At home folding a letter to Luther.. the first warning came through the window
  t.any.2 Put bread in a cloth before choosing which road to take
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_FAMILY
  gate.rule trust>=10
  t.any.1 Nola and I fostered.. Philip vanished at our picnic in sixty-one.. she asked for a head count and I waved her off to finish announcements.. never found him.. still blame myself
  fx.1 reveal f_philip
  fx.2 set flag:philip_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_FAMILY.d
  t.any.1 Luther was one of our foster boys.. he's grown with a trade now
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_FAMILY.d2
  t.any.1 The other names aren't a list I'm handing out
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_FIRSTJOB
  t.any.1 Cecil had me fetching repair parts.. more fetching than fixing
  t.any.2 First proper wages came from factory work.. gave Dovie half before she asked
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_HOBBY
  t.any.1 Carving spoons when nobody was asking for a visit
  t.any.2 Still carry a half-made one.. finish it if the road gives me an evening
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_HOUSE
  t.any.1 Parsonage.. too few hooks and too many coats
  t.any.2 Tap dripped over a chipped basin.. Luther knew it by the sound
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_LASTNORMAL
  t.any.1 Argued with a man over who'd left chairs in the aisle
  t.any.2 Expected to finish the spoon after supper.. kept planning that evening for days
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_LOVE
  t.any.1 Nola.. met her taking chairs back after a service
  t.any.2 Married in fifty-three.. she made me learn to ask instead of announce
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_MONEY
  gate.rule trust>=70 & alone & flag:nola_told
  t.any.1 Have eighty dollars hidden.. sold Nola's wedding ring this spring.. kept asking the church for truck expenses without telling them I had that cash.. wanted their money before using hers
  fx.1 reveal f_ring
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_MONEY.d
  t.any.1 Truck expenses were the worry.. leave the purse closed
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_MONEY.d2
  t.any.1 No.. won't turn Nola's things into a public account
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_PARENTS
  t.any.1 Dovie saved bread.. Cecil repaired anything people would bring him
  t.any.2 Both gone.. mother would've had something to say about this jacket
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_PROUD
  t.any.1 Luther teaching someone else his trade.. remembered him losing every screw he touched
  t.any.2 A spoon Nola actually chose over the bought ones
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  t.any.1 Local school first.. preaching lessons later in other men's kitchens
  t.any.2 Better at reciting than sitting an examination.. Nola noticed immediately
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_SIBLING
  t.any.1 No brother left living.. Mose is my cousin
  t.any.2 Mose handled snakes in his church.. I took supper with him, never part in that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_SPOUSE
  t.any.1 Nola Logsdon.. wrote smaller than anyone I've ever known
  t.any.2 Could disagree with me while handing me another biscuit
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_WORK
  gate.rule trust>=40 & flag:local_told
  t.any.1 Baptist preacher and factory hand.. condemned the sixty-eight strike in church.. then paid groceries for three striking households out of my wages.. couldn't admit they had a case
  fx.1 reveal f_strike
  fx.2 set flag:strike_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_WORK.d
  t.any.1 Preached and took factory shifts.. household needed both
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_PAST_WORK.d2
  t.any.1 There's a strike story behind that.. won't polish it for you today
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Sixty-three.. Dovie was younger than that when I began calling her old
  t.any.2 Born in thirty.. jacket came along considerably later
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_COMFORT
  t.any.1 Wood under the knife.. a spoon doesn't need reassuring
  t.any.2 Hear me plain.. sometimes I need someone to tell me they're staying
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 A microphone turned up enough to hide a poor argument
  t.any.2 Bread thrown out because the heel isn't pretty
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.any.1 Luther's the last one I know how to look for.. fear there's nobody at that workshop
  t.any.2 Losing the last person who can tell me to hush and mean it kindly
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 Beans with yesterday's bread.. leave some heel
  t.any.2 Dovie's corn pudding.. nobody could reproduce the burnt corner
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_FROM
  gate.rule trust>=25 & flag:philip_told
  t.any.1 Elizabethtown.. born there and never really left.. told people I was passing through so families I'd preached at wouldn't recognize me.. wasn't a traveler at all
  cb.1 Still the Elizabethtown preacher.. no passing-through tale between us now
  fx.1 reveal f_local
  fx.2 set flag:local_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_FROM.d
  t.any.1 Elizabethtown roads.. let that stand for now
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_FROM.d2
  t.any.1 Don't need the whole address read back to me
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Leave some heel.. Dovie's rule got into my hands
  t.any.2 Folding the bread cloth.. nothing in it has to be there for me to fold it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.any.1 Hold a place at Luther's table.. I'll settle for standing beside it
  t.any.2 That pickup starting after I get fuel.. been asking the Lord for smaller things lately
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Feet sore and still hungry
  t.lo.2 Slept in a truck.. don't recommend the seat belt buckle
  t.mid.1 Hear me plain.. I'd like a stop longer than a roadside prayer
  t.mid.2 Nola would've made me take this jacket off by now
  t.mid.3 Ask Jeremiah, not the man who ought to have a word for everybody
  t.mid.4 I don't have a sermon for that. Might be a relief to both of us
  t.mid.5 Better hearing a question you mean than a blessing you don't
  t.hi.1 Tired enough to ask you to stop fussing and let me rest
  t.hi.2 Could use company that doesn't call me Reverend
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 Carving spoons.. useful even when they're ugly
  t.any.2 Nola reading while I worked at the kitchen table
  t.any.3 Somebody singing because they like the song, not because I'm watching
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Nola at the piano without anybody calling a number
  t.any.2 A low hymn.. once the high voices settle down
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Jeremiah Logsdon.. Jeremiah indoors please
  t.any.2 Logsdon.. same as the man who talks too loud at the church
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_PRAYER
  t.any.1 Yes.. not offering you a demonstration
  t.any.2 Pray for Luther most mornings.. then look for fuel
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Please.. pulpit voice can take its coat off too
  t.any.2 No sermon required from either of us
  t.any.3 Yes. Let me sit with a thought before I start telling you what it means
  t.any.4 Quiet together would be welcome. Don't make a service of it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Truck cab for a few hours.. kept waking against the door handle
  t.any.2 Dream of the parsonage tap dripping.. used to curse that little sound
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.any.1 Luther kept a spoon I carved with a hole through the bowl.. called it his soup examiner.. Nola served stew with it once and said his examination was taking too long
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Rain would soak the bread cloth.. hope it holds off
  t.any.2 Mose could smell rain before I saw a cloud
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_WORLD_BITTEN
  t.any.1 Keep away from a bite.. but don't make a show of the person suffering it
  t.any.2 Would give space and keep talking if they could hear.. wouldn't offer a cure
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_WORLD_CHURCH
  t.any.1 No current word of an open church.. mine's behind me now
  t.any.2 A door with a cross isn't an invitation unless someone answers
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_WORLD_CITY
  t.any.1 Haven't seen Louisville since this began.. still reckon cities are worse for finding a quiet way out
  t.any.2 City crowds frighten me more than county roads.. that's a preference, not a report
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_WORLD_DEAD
  t.any.1 People.. knew someone's supper table before they came to this
  t.any.2 Still somebody's family.. being afraid doesn't change that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 No word from Luther's place.. people keep giving me other workshops
  t.any.2 Heard fuel was being moved.. man couldn't name a truck he'd seen
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.VQ_WORLD_TRUCKS
  t.any.1 My red pickup's back along the road.. saw one other truck with a canvas load, didn't see where it turned
  t.any.2 Yes.. two farm trucks passed while I was walking.. neither stopped and I couldn't read a name
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1097.leave.angry
  t.any.1 Enough.. Jeremiah's leaving without a closing prayer
  t.any.2 Don't need an amen to end this.. goodbye
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1097.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Keys accounted for.. ought to get back along the road
  t.any.2 Bread cloth folded.. I'll leave the chair where it is
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1097.react.gave_blanket
  gate.rule gave:blanket
  t.any.1 Nola would've said keep this dry before anything else
  t.any.2 Useful thing to spare.. won't dismiss it as a little favor
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1097.react.gave_food
  gate.rule gave:food
  t.any.1 Lord knows I needed that.. thank you
  t.any.2 Jeremiah accepts.. no speech before eating
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1097.react.gave_water
  gate.rule gave:water
  t.any.1 Water's welcome.. cloth stays clear of it
  t.any.2 Throat might thank you more clearly than I do
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1097.react.insult
  t.any.1 No pulpit here.. say it without expecting me to stand and take it
  t.any.2 Jeremiah heard you.. Reverend has nothing to add
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1097.react.refused
  t.any.1 Then it's no.. sermon won't buy a different answer
  t.any.2 I'll ask elsewhere.. won't spend your time arguing
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1097.react.threat
  t.any.1 Keys remain in my pocket.. I'm not coming nearer
  t.any.2 Hold on!.. tell me which way you want me to go
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1097.return.arrive
  gate.rule visits>=1
  t.any.1 Jeremiah again.. same jacket, no new sermon
  t.any.2 Found your place before I unfolded Luther's directions
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1097.return.gave_food
  gate.rule visits>=1 & gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Didn't forget the food.. better memory than most church notices
  t.any.2 Knew which house had helped when this road came round again
  tag.1 kind:return
end
